---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { contactEmail } from "../lib/legal";
---

<LegalLayout
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="The terms for using and paying for PulseBoard."
    lang="en"
    alternate="/pl/terms"
>
    <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
    <p>
        PulseBoard is an online service for uploading server metrics in CSV
        format and viewing them as dashboards. It is provided by PulseBoard
        ("we", "us"). You can contact us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        These terms set out the rules for using PulseBoard and serve as the
        terms of electronically supplied services under the Polish Act on
        Providing Services by Electronic Means. They are available in Polish and
        English. If the two versions differ, the Polish version prevails. How we
        handle personal data is described in our{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        A <strong>consumer</strong> is a person buying for purposes not related
        to their business or profession. The consumer rules in these terms
        (sections 7 and 8 and the consumer parts of section 10) also apply to a
        sole trader who buys PulseBoard for a purpose that is not professional
        in nature for them, as defined in the Polish Consumer Rights Act.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Account and technical requirements</h2>
    <p>
        To use PulseBoard you need an account. You can register with an email
        address and password, or with Google or Facebook. You must confirm your
        email address before buying a licence. You must give accurate
        information, keep your password secret and are responsible for activity
        on your account.
    </p>
    <p>
        You need an internet connection, an up-to-date web browser with
        JavaScript and cookies enabled, and an email account. Creating an
        account is free. A contract for the free account is concluded when you
        register and lasts until you or we end it under section 11.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Plans, prices and payment</h2>
    <p>Using the dashboards requires a paid licence. We offer:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Subscription</strong>: 19 PLN per month, billed monthly in
            advance;
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Lifetime licence</strong>: a one-time payment of 199 PLN.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Both give access to all PulseBoard features. Prices are final prices in
        Polish zloty (PLN), including any taxes due. Payments are processed by
        Stripe; you can pay with the methods shown at checkout. The contract for
        a licence is concluded when your payment is confirmed, and you can use
        your licence immediately afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Licences, renewal and cancellation</h2>
    <p>
        Your licence is personal: you may use PulseBoard for your own purposes
        or those of your business, but you may not resell or share access to
        your account.
    </p>
    <h3>Subscription</h3>
    <p>
        The subscription renews automatically every month and Stripe charges
        your payment method at the start of each period until you cancel. You
        can cancel at any time in the Stripe Customer Portal, which you open
        with the <strong>Manage subscription</strong> button on the plans page.
        You can also update your payment method there. After cancelling, you
        keep access until the end of the period you have already paid for, and
        you will not be charged again. We do not refund partial months, except
        where the law requires it.
    </p>
    <p>
        If a renewal payment fails, Stripe may retry it. If it still cannot be
        collected, your subscription ends and paid features are locked until you
        subscribe again. Your datasets are kept until you delete them.
    </p>
    <p>
        We may change the subscription price for future periods. We will tell
        you by email at least 30 days before the new price applies to you, and
        you may cancel before then.
    </p>
    <h3>Lifetime licence</h3>
    <p>
        The lifetime licence gives you access for as long as we operate
        PulseBoard, without further payments. If you buy it while you have an
        active subscription, we cancel the subscription automatically.
    </p>
    <h3>Deleting your account</h3>
    <p>
        You can delete your account at any time in account settings. This ends
        the contract, cancels any active subscription and permanently deletes
        your data, as described in the Privacy Policy. Deleting the account does
        not by itself entitle you to a refund.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Upload limits</h2>
    <p>Each account can store:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>up to 5 datasets at a time;</li>
        <li>CSV files of up to 25 MB each;</li>
        <li>up to 500,000 rows per file.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Files that go over these limits or do not match the expected CSV format
        are rejected. We may change these limits. If we lower them, data you
        have already uploaded will not be deleted because of the change.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You must not:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>upload data you do not have the right to use;</li>
        <li>
            upload unlawful content, malware or personal data of others without
            a legal basis;
        </li>
        <li>
            try to access other users' accounts or data, or test, bypass or
            break our security or rate limits;
        </li>
        <li>
            overload the service, for example with automated mass requests, or
            interfere with other users' use of it;
        </li>
        <li>
            copy, resell or reverse engineer the service, except where the law
            allows it.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        You remain the owner of the data you upload. You allow us to store and
        process it only to provide PulseBoard to you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="withdrawal">7. Right of withdrawal (consumers)</h2>
    <p>
        As a consumer you normally have the right to withdraw from a contract
        concluded at a distance within 14 days of concluding it, without giving
        a reason.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>
            Before checkout we ask you to expressly agree that we start
            supplying PulseBoard immediately, before the 14-day period ends, and
            to acknowledge that you thereby lose your right of withdrawal.
            Checkout is not available without this consent. Once you have given
            it and your paid access has started, you lose the right to withdraw
            from that purchase
        </strong>{" "}
        (Art. 38(1)(13) of the Polish Consumer Rights Act). We keep a record of
        when you gave this consent.
    </p>
    <p>
        If, despite this, mandatory law gives you a right to withdraw from a
        contract whose performance has already started at your request, you will
        pay for what was supplied until you withdraw, in proportion to the full
        price.
    </p>
    <p>
        Where the right of withdrawal applies, you can use it by sending us a
        clear statement by email to{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> before the period
        ends. You can use this model form, but you do not have to:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
        <p>
            To: PulseBoard, {contactEmail}
            <br />
            I hereby give notice that I withdraw from my contract for the
            following service: PulseBoard (subscription / lifetime licence).
            <br />
            Ordered on: …<br />
            Name and email address of the account: …<br />
            Date: …
        </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
        We will refund any amount due within 14 days of receiving your
        statement, using the payment method you used, at no cost to you.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
        If PulseBoard does not work as described in these terms, you can file a
        complaint by email to{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Please describe
        the problem and tell us the email address of your account. We will reply
        within 14 days. Consumers have the rights set out in the Polish Consumer
        Rights Act for digital content and digital services that do not conform
        to the contract, including the right to have them brought into
        conformity, to a price reduction or to terminate the contract.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you are a consumer, you may also use out-of-court ways of resolving
        complaints, for example by contacting a municipal or district consumer
        ombudsman (miejski lub powiatowy rzecznik konsumentów) or the Provincial
        Inspectorate of Trade Inspection (Wojewódzki Inspektorat Inspekcji
        Handlowej). More information is available at{" "}
        <a href="https://uokik.gov.pl" rel="noopener">
            uokik.gov.pl
        </a>
        .
    </p>

    <h2>9. Availability and changes to the service</h2>
    <p>
        We aim to keep PulseBoard available at all times, but there may be
        breaks for maintenance, updates or failures outside our control. We may
        improve and change features, provided the paid service keeps the
        features described in these terms or the changes do not make it worse
        for you.
    </p>
    <p>
        We back up our database regularly, but PulseBoard is not a backup
        service. Please keep your own copies of the CSV files you upload.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Liability</h2>
    <p>
        PulseBoard displays the data you upload. It does not monitor your
        servers, and any forecasts are estimates. You are responsible for
        decisions you make based on it.
    </p>
    <p>
        Towards business customers who are not covered by the consumer rules,
        our liability is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months
        before the event that caused the damage, and we are not liable for lost
        profits or lost data.
    </p>
    <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our liability where the law
        does not allow it, including for damage caused intentionally, and
        nothing limits the rights consumers have under mandatory law.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Ending the contract</h2>
    <p>
        You can end the contract at any time by deleting your account. We may
        suspend or close an account that seriously or repeatedly breaks these
        terms, after warning you by email where possible. If we close an account
        with a paid licence for a reason other than your breach of these terms,
        including if we stop operating PulseBoard, we will tell you at least 30
        days in advance and refund the unused part of a subscription period.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
        We may change these terms for important reasons, such as changes in the
        law, in our services or in how we provide them. We will tell you by
        email at least 14 days before the changes take effect. If you do not
        accept them, you can cancel your subscription or delete your account
        before then. Changes do not affect purchases already made.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
        These terms are governed by Polish law. If you are a consumer living in
        another EU country, you also keep the protection of the mandatory
        consumer laws of that country. Disputes will be settled by the court
        with jurisdiction under the general rules of law.
    </p>
</LegalLayout>
